Round 57: X-Tenant-Id header parity across all SDKs

Backend reads X-Tenant-Id header (Round 51) before falling back to
body tenant_id. Until now every SDK only embedded tenant in the
JSON envelope, which works but costs a body parse before routing.

- Go SDK: WithTenantHeader option on the Exporter attaches
  X-Tenant-Id; exporter_tenant_test.go exercises it
- Node SDK: _post() adds X-Tenant-Id when tenant is configured;
  tenant_test.js verifies against a local HTTP server
- Python SDK: _post() adds X-Tenant-Id when tenant is configured;
  tenant_test.py verifies it
- Java SDK: HttpRequest.Builder emits X-Tenant-Id only when tenant
  is non-empty (stdlib http client does not permit empty values)

Also ran the route-vs-caller diff; frontend now covers every
backend route that is meaningful to the UI. Backend-only routes
that remain are SDK receivers (/v1/{logs,metrics,traces}, /api/ingest/*,
/api/prom/write, /api/v1/write, /api/seed*, /api/stream, /api/export,
/api/v1/query, /metrics) and a few pprof/internal mounts.
